@startuml
title Bounded AI Research Investigation

actor User
participant "Investigation panel" as UI
participant "AI research routes" as API
participant "Investigation service\n(serial queue)" as Orchestrator
database "PostgreSQL\njobs, passages, disclosure metadata" as DB
participant "Bounded typed tools" as Tools
participant "Restricted analysis runtime" as Analysis
participant "Local Ollama" as Ollama
participant "Egress helper\n(short-lived process)" as Egress
participant "OpenAI Responses API" as OpenAI

User -> UI: Select scope, depth, language,\nresearch mode, route, and approved API model
UI -> API: POST /investigations
API -> Orchestrator: Strict typed request
Orchestrator -> DB: Persist queued job
alt Material ambiguity
  Orchestrator -> DB: Persist waiting plan
  UI --> User: Request clarification and typed date scope
else Scope is sufficient
  alt Selected-evidence cloud synthesis
    User -> UI: Enter exact task and evidence
    User -> UI: Inspect exact synthesis payload
    UI -> API: Create dedicated digest-bound grant
    API -> DB: Reserve disclosure and spend budgets
    Orchestrator -> DB: Checkpoint selected evidence
  else Local planning
    Orchestrator -> Ollama: Candidate step identifiers
    Ollama --> Orchestrator: Prioritized identifiers
  else Opt-in OpenAI planning
    User -> UI: Inspect exact outbound planning payload
    UI -> API: Create digest-bound grant
    API -> DB: Reserve disclosure and spend budgets
    Orchestrator -> Egress: Canonical allowlisted planning payload\nwith selected model and its price
    Egress -> OpenAI: POST /v1/responses\nstore=false, tools=[]
    OpenAI --> Egress: Prioritized identifiers, catalog plans, and usage
    Egress --> Orchestrator: Bounded response
  end
  Orchestrator -> DB: Persist constrained plan
end
alt Selected-evidence cloud synthesis
  Orchestrator -> Egress: Canonical selected-evidence payload\nwith selected model and its price
  Egress -> OpenAI: POST /v1/responses\nstore=false, tools=[]
  OpenAI --> Egress: Structured final answer and usage
  Egress --> Orchestrator: Bounded response
else Local evidence workflow
  loop Each incomplete step
    alt Cloud-authored catalog analysis step
      Orchestrator -> Analysis: Validate catalog and workspace; inject trusted scope
      Analysis --> Orchestrator: Private local rows or explicit failure
    else Locally authored tool step
      Orchestrator -> Tools: Dispatch allowlisted tool with caps
      Tools --> Orchestrator: Evidence or explicit partial failure
    end
    Orchestrator -> DB: Checkpoint step result
  end

  opt Detailed mode has failed local steps
    Orchestrator -> Ollama: Inspect partial evidence and failed local candidates
    Ollama --> Orchestrator: Select up to three retry identifiers
    Orchestrator -> Tools: One serial local retry pass
    Orchestrator -> DB: Checkpoint revised plan and retry results
  end

  Orchestrator -> Ollama: Selected local evidence only
  Ollama --> Orchestrator: Structured answer candidate
end

Orchestrator -> Orchestrator: Validate citations and answer schema
Orchestrator -> DB: Complete, partial, failed, or cancelled
API --> UI: Facts, calculations, interpretations,\ngaps, conflicts, and evidence
UI --> User: Inspectable evidence-backed answer

note right of Orchestrator
One active job bounds CPU and RAM.
External checkpoints are never replayed by the retry loop.
No automatic cloud fallback.
Financial calculations use deterministic services.
Cloud synthesis receives only manually selected evidence.
Cloud planning receives identifiers, never relations, SQL, private scope IDs, or rows.
Cloud-authored analysis rows remain private and are synthesized locally.
Selected models come from the server allowlist.
Per-model prices drive spend reservation.
end note

@enduml
